       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks like an error, so I need you to confirm it first.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 1700 mg PO TID, which is 5,100 mg/day.\n- **Maximum labeled dose:** 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Single doses are usually capped at about 1,000 mg, and 850 mg TID is a common regimen. The ordered daily dose is twice the maximum.\n- **Risk:** A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders include:\n- 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day)\n- 1,000 mg PO BID with meals (2,000 mg/day)\n- 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO TID with meals\n- 1,700 mg total per day, split into doses (for example, 850 mg BID)\n\nTell me the dose you intended, or confirm that 1,700 mg TID is deliberate. If it is deliberate, please give me the clinical rationale to put in the order note. Once you reply, I'll enter the order right away."
      }
